Subject: [PATCH] feat(models): named generation projections (M1e)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A class has one anchoring model and several generation projections
(spec 16 §2, 14 §18). kimun.surface.models.generate/project writes a named
projection in :markdown, :edn or :json from the captured payload, filtered
by :fields and inherited through :base; :markdown/v1 of a v1 descriptor is
render/render. A projection never changes what was captured.

:mode and :sugar, which the fixture uses and the spec does not define, are
refused with a typed error. The Markdown layout written from :fields is not
fixed by the spec: it is an executor's choice, pending the owner.

Implemented by a sonnet executor.
Evidence: runs/subagents/2026-11-15-M1e/.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
